From: noemdespertis <noemdespertis@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: venus: support the sm7150, and enable it on the surya

The POCO X3 NFC decodes every video in software: the Venus node
(qcom,sm7150-venus) is disabled in sm7150.dtsi, and even enabled nothing
would bind to it, because the driver has no entry for the sm7150. The
sm7150-mainline tree stopped at the node ("WIP! arm64: dts: qcom: sm7150:
Add venus node") and left `&venus { //status = "okay"; }` commented out.

Everything else is already there: CONFIG_VIDEO_QCOM_VENUS=m, videocc-sm7150,
the interconnects, venus.mbn under qcom/sm7150/xiaomi/surya/ with the
firmware-name pointing at it, and a reserved region at 0x93400000 identical
to Xiaomi's pil_video_region.

What the hardware is. Xiaomi's sdmmagpie-vidc.dtsi has ONE video core on
MVS0 (vcodec-supply = mvs0_gdsc); MVS1 is the CVP (cvp-supply), not a second
codec. The HFI is 4.x like the sc7180. But msm_vidc_platform.c puts the
sc7180 (atoll), sm6150 and sdm845 on VPU_VERSION_4 and the sdmmagpie together
with the sm8150 on VPU_VERSION_5 -- the generation mainline calls IRIS1 and
has an enum for but no user. The firmware agrees: it reports itself as
"14:VIDEO.IR.1.2-00054-PROD-1" on a wrapper of hw version 5.11.20a. So:
sc7180's resources (one vcodec, HFI 4XX) with .vpu_version =
VPU_VERSION_IRIS1, and the things the downstream driver does only for VPU 5.

Measured on the phone, 2026-09-19, by editing the installed DTB and loading
the module by hand. With "qcom,sc7180-venus": TZ authenticates venus.mbn,
the firmware boots and answers SYS_INIT 100 ms later, and then the first
power collapse fails:

    wait for cpu and video core idle fail (-110)

The same with "qcom,sdm845-venus-v2". With a first cut of this patch
(IRIS1 profile, CGC config, interrupt mask, DSP queue registers) the probe
completes and /dev/video10-11 appear, but the two status bits read

    cpu status 0x0, ctrl status 0x1

and a decoder session gets no answer at all: SESSION_INIT times out, the
Venus interrupt count does not move. The firmware answers SYS_INIT and
then nothing, and never reaches WFI.

The difference that fits: WHEN the video core is powered. In mainline's v4
path, core_power_v4() powers only the venus GDSC and the core clocks; the
vcodec0 domain and its clocks are brought up per session (poweron_coreid),
and the sc7180 firmware is happy to boot with the video core off. Downstream
enables every GDSC (mvsc, mvs0, mvs1) and hands them to hardware control
BEFORE loading the firmware, and keeps the CVP clock in the proxy set. An
IRIS1 firmware that initialises the video core and the CVP at boot has
nothing to talk to. So on IRIS1 both vcodec domains are powered with the
core, clocks on, and handed to hardware control (HW_CTRL_TRIGGER is set on
both in videocc-sm7150); sessions still only take core 1.

The other VPU 5 differences are carried too, as downstream has them:
WRAPPER_CPU_CGC_DIS and WRAPPER_CPU_CLOCK_CONFIG written to 0 on power on
(mainline does that only on the no-TZ path), the interrupt mask unmasked
bit by bit (A2HCPU and A2HWD) instead of written to 0x8, and the DSP view of
the queue table (CPU_CS_VMIMSG, VMIMSGAG0, VMIMSGAG1) pointed at the CPU
queues, since there is no CVP client. None of those alone changed the
status bits.

For the next time this fails: the idle timeout prints both status
registers, and on IRIS1 returns -EAGAIN instead of -ETIMEDOUT. Downstream
treats a busy core as "skip power collapse, try later"; -EAGAIN is the
runtime-PM spelling of that, whereas -ETIMEDOUT sets runtime_error and
leaves the device unusable until it is unbound. The probe tolerates that
-EAGAIN. The F/W version parser learns the "VIDEO.IR" form.

Clock table: the three rates of the sm7150 OPP table (240/338/365 MHz),
which are also the only ones Xiaomi allows. Bandwidth tables are the
sc7180's until measured.

Enabled in sm7150-xiaomi-surya.dtsi, not in the common dtsi: this tree
only tests on the surya.

Sources, so every claim above can be checked:

  Mainline (sm7150-mainline/linux, tag v7.1_rc3 -- the tree this aport builds):
    https://github.com/sm7150-mainline/linux/tree/v7.1_rc3
    arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7150.dtsi            venus node, status = "disabled"
    arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7150-xiaomi-common.dtsi   `&venus { //status = "okay"; }`
    arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7150-xiaomi-surya.dtsi    firmware-name
    commit 266961c24e57 "WIP! arm64: dts: qcom: sm7150: Add venus node"
    drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/core.c        venus_dt_match, sc7180_res, sdm845_res_v2
    drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/core.h        enum vpu_version (IRIS1 unused), IS_IRIS1()
    drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/hfi_venus.c   venus_boot_core, venus_run, venus_power_on,
                                                    venus_suspend_3xx, venus_cpu_and_video_core_idle
    drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/hfi_venus_io.h  CPU_CS_*, WRAPPER_* offsets
    drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/hfi_msgs.c    sys_get_prop_image_version
    drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/firmware.c    venus_reset_cpu (CGC on the no-TZ path),
                                                    firmware-name override
    drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/pm_helpers.c  core_power_v4, poweron_coreid, vcodec_control_v4
    drivers/clk/qcom/videocc-sm7150.c               vcodec0/1 GDSCs with HW_CTRL_TRIGGER
    include/dt-bindings/clock/qcom,sm7150-videocc.h

  Xiaomi's kernel for this phone (MiCode/Xiaomi_Kernel_OpenSource, branch surya-q-oss):
    https://github.com/MiCode/Xiaomi_Kernel_OpenSource/tree/surya-q-oss
    arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdmmagpie-vidc.dtsi    one vcodec (mvs0), cvp-supply = mvs1,
                                                    the seven clocks, allowed-clock-rates
    arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdmmagpie.dtsi         pil_video_region@93400000
    drivers/media/platform/msm/vidc/msm_vidc_platform.c   sdmmagpie = VPU_VERSION_5,
                                                    sc7180/sm6150/sdm845 = VPU_VERSION_4,
                                                    sdmmagpie_common_data (power-collapse-delay,
                                                    sw-power-collapse, domain-cvp, max-hw-load)
    drivers/media/platform/msm/vidc/venus_hfi.c     vpu5_ops: interrupt_init_vpu5,
                                                    setup_dsp_uc_memmap_vpu5,
                                                    clock_config_on_enable_vpu5;
                                                    __power_collapse (same idle registers);
                                                    __enable_regulators / __hand_off_regulators;
                                                    venus_hfi_core_init (what is sent after SYS_INIT)
    drivers/media/platform/msm/vidc/vidc_hfi_io.h   VIDC_CPU_CS_VMIMSG*, VIDC_WRAPPER_CPU_STATUS,
                                                    VIDC_WRAPPER_CPU_CGC_DIS, ..._CLOCK_CONFIG

  Measurements: all on a POCO X3 NFC (Huaxing), postmarketOS, this aport at r266..r267,
  2026-09-19. The DTB experiments used fdtput on the installed
  sm7150-xiaomi-surya-huaxing.dtb with the module blacklisted and loaded by hand;
  the decode checks are ffmpeg's h264/hevc/vp9_v4l2m2m against its software decoders
  through the psnr filter (inf = identical), and mpv 0.41 with --hwdec=v4l2m2m-copy.

Signed-off-by: noemdespertis <noemdespertis@gmail.com>
---
diff -ruN a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7150-xiaomi-surya.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7150-xiaomi-surya.dtsi
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7150-xiaomi-surya.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7150-xiaomi-surya.dtsi
@@ -454,6 +454,7 @@
 
 &venus {
 	firmware-name = "qcom/sm7150/xiaomi/surya/venus.mbn";
+	status = "okay";
 };
 
 &vreg_l18a_2p8 {
diff -ruN a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/core.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/core.c
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/core.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/core.c
@@ -496,7 +496,13 @@
 		goto err_of_depopulate;
 
 	ret = pm_runtime_put_sync(dev);
-	if (ret) {
+	if (ret == -EAGAIN) {
+		/*
+		 * The core was still busy (IRIS1 says so instead of failing):
+		 * it stays powered and the suspend is retried on the next put.
+		 */
+		ret = 0;
+	} else if (ret) {
 		pm_runtime_get_noresume(dev);
 		goto err_of_depopulate;
 	}
@@ -949,6 +955,54 @@
 	.enc_nodename = "video-encoder",
 };
 
+/* The rates the sm7150 OPP table allows; Xiaomi's tree lists the same three. */
+static const struct freq_tbl sm7150_freq_table[] = {
+	{ 0, 365000000 },
+	{ 0, 338000000 },
+	{ 0, 240000000 },
+};
+
+/*
+ * SM7150 (Snapdragon 730/732): one video core on VCODEC0; the second MVS core
+ * is the CVP, which the firmware also drives, so it is powered along with the
+ * core but never given a session. HFI 4.x like the sc7180, but the VPU is the
+ * sm8150 generation (downstream VPU_VERSION_5, "IRIS1"), which needs the IRIS1
+ * handling in hfi_venus.c and pm_helpers.c. Bandwidth tables borrowed from
+ * the sc7180 until measured.
+ */
+static const struct venus_resources sm7150_res = {
+	.freq_tbl = sm7150_freq_table,
+	.freq_tbl_size = ARRAY_SIZE(sm7150_freq_table),
+	.bw_tbl_enc = sc7180_bw_table_enc,
+	.bw_tbl_enc_size = ARRAY_SIZE(sc7180_bw_table_enc),
+	.bw_tbl_dec = sc7180_bw_table_dec,
+	.bw_tbl_dec_size = ARRAY_SIZE(sc7180_bw_table_dec),
+	.clks = {"core", "iface", "bus" },
+	.clks_num = 3,
+	.vcodec0_clks = { "vcodec0_core", "vcodec0_bus" },
+	.vcodec1_clks = { "vcodec1_core", "vcodec1_bus" },
+	.vcodec_clks_num = 2,
+	.vcodec_pmdomains = (const char *[]) { "venus", "vcodec0", "vcodec1" },
+	.vcodec_pmdomains_num = 3,
+	.opp_pmdomain = (const char *[]) { "cx" },
+	/* Sessions only ever go to core 1; core 2 is the CVP, see core_power_v4 */
+	.vcodec_num = 1,
+	.max_load = 3110400,	/* 4096x2160@90 */
+	.hfi_version = HFI_VERSION_4XX,
+	.vpu_version = VPU_VERSION_IRIS1,
+	.vmem_id = VIDC_RESOURCE_NONE,
+	.vmem_size = 0,
+	.vmem_addr = 0,
+	.dma_mask = 0xe0000000 - 1,
+	.cp_start = 0,
+	.cp_size = 0x70800000,
+	.cp_nonpixel_start = 0x1000000,
+	.cp_nonpixel_size = 0x24800000,
+	.fwname = "qcom/sm7150/venus.mbn",
+	.dec_nodename = "video-decoder",
+	.enc_nodename = "video-encoder",
+};
+
 static const struct freq_tbl sm8250_freq_table[] = {
 	{ 0, 444000000 },
 	{ 0, 366000000 },
@@ -1129,6 +1183,7 @@
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sdm660-venus", .data = &sdm660_res, },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sdm845-venus", .data = &sdm845_res, },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sdm845-venus-v2", .data = &sdm845_res_v2, },
+	{ .compatible = "qcom,sm7150-venus", .data = &sm7150_res, },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sm8250-venus", .data = &sm8250_res, },
 	{ }
 };
diff -ruN a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/hfi_msgs.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/hfi_msgs.c
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/hfi_msgs.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/hfi_msgs.c
@@ -321,7 +321,13 @@
 	if (ret)
 		goto done;
 
-	dev_err(dev, VDBGL "error reading F/W version\n");
+	/* IRIS1 (sm7150): "14:VIDEO.IR.1.2-00054-PROD-1" */
+	ret = sscanf(img_ver, "14:VIDEO.IR.%u.%u-%u",
+		     &core->venus_ver.major, &core->venus_ver.minor, &core->venus_ver.rev);
+	if (ret)
+		goto done;
+
+	dev_err(dev, VDBGL "error reading F/W version (%s)\n", (const char *)img_ver);
 	return;
 
 done:
diff -ruN a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/hfi_venus.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/hfi_venus.c
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/hfi_venus.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/hfi_venus.c
@@ -477,6 +477,17 @@
 		mask_val = readl(wrapper_base + WRAPPER_INTR_MASK);
 		mask_val &= ~(WRAPPER_INTR_MASK_A2HWD_BASK_V6 |
 			      WRAPPER_INTR_MASK_A2HCPU_MASK);
+	} else if (IS_IRIS1(hdev->core)) {
+		/*
+		 * Like IRIS2: unmask only the CPU and watchdog lines and keep
+		 * the rest of the reset value. This is what the downstream
+		 * driver does for its VPU 5 (interrupt_init_vpu5), where
+		 * the AR50 write below would also unmask lines it never
+		 * handles.
+		 */
+		mask_val = readl(wrapper_base + WRAPPER_INTR_MASK);
+		mask_val &= ~(WRAPPER_INTR_MASK_A2HWD_BASK |
+			      WRAPPER_INTR_MASK_A2HCPU_MASK);
 	} else {
 		mask_val = WRAPPER_INTR_MASK_A2HVCODEC_MASK;
 	}
@@ -544,6 +555,17 @@
 
 	writel(hdev->ifaceq_table.da, cpu_cs_base + UC_REGION_ADDR);
 	writel(SHARED_QSIZE, cpu_cs_base + UC_REGION_SIZE);
+	if (IS_IRIS1(hdev->core)) {
+		/*
+		 * IRIS1 firmware also serves a DSP (CVP) client and keeps a
+		 * second view of the queue table for it. Downstream
+		 * (setup_dsp_uc_memmap_vpu5) points it at the CPU queues
+		 * when there is no CVP client, as here.
+		 */
+		writel(hdev->ifaceq_table.da, cpu_cs_base + CPU_CS_VMIMSG);
+		writel(hdev->ifaceq_table.da, cpu_cs_base + CPU_CS_VMIMSGAG0);
+		writel(SHARED_QSIZE, cpu_cs_base + CPU_CS_VMIMSGAG1);
+	}
 	writel(hdev->ifaceq_table.da, cpu_cs_base + CPU_CS_SCIACMDARG2);
 	writel(0x01, cpu_cs_base + CPU_CS_SCIACMDARG1);
 	if (hdev->sfr.da)
@@ -674,6 +696,22 @@
 	if (ret)
 		goto err;
 
+	if (IS_IRIS1(hdev->core)) {
+		void __iomem *wrapper_base = hdev->core->wrapper_base;
+
+		/*
+		 * Downstream writes these after every clock enable, and only
+		 * on VPU 5 (clock_config_on_enable_vpu5). Mainline writes
+		 * them only on the non-TZ path (venus_reset_cpu), which a
+		 * production phone never takes: TZ boots the firmware. Left
+		 * at their reset values, the ARM9 on the sm7150 answered
+		 * SYS_INIT but never showed WFI in WRAPPER_CPU_STATUS, and
+		 * the first power collapse timed out (measured 2026-09-19).
+		 */
+		writel(0x0, wrapper_base + WRAPPER_CPU_CGC_DIS);
+		writel(0x0, wrapper_base + WRAPPER_CPU_CLOCK_CONFIG);
+	}
+
 	ret = venus_run(hdev);
 	if (ret)
 		goto err_suspend;
@@ -1539,6 +1577,16 @@
 	return 0;
 }
 
+static u32 venus_cpu_status(struct venus_hfi_device *hdev)
+{
+	struct venus_core *core = hdev->core;
+
+	if (IS_IRIS2(core) || IS_IRIS2_1(core) || IS_AR50_LITE(core))
+		return readl(core->wrapper_tz_base + WRAPPER_TZ_CPU_STATUS_V6);
+
+	return readl(core->wrapper_base + WRAPPER_CPU_STATUS);
+}
+
 static bool venus_cpu_and_video_core_idle(struct venus_hfi_device *hdev)
 {
 	void __iomem *wrapper_base = hdev->core->wrapper_base;
@@ -1615,7 +1663,17 @@
 	ret = readx_poll_timeout(venus_cpu_and_video_core_idle, hdev, val, val,
 				 1500, 100 * 1500);
 	if (ret) {
-		dev_err(dev, "wait for cpu and video core idle fail (%d)\n", ret);
+		dev_err(dev, "wait for cpu and video core idle fail (%d): cpu status %#x, ctrl status %#x\n",
+			ret, venus_cpu_status(hdev),
+			readl(cpu_cs_base + CPU_CS_SCIACMDARG0));
+		/*
+		 * A core that is still busy is not an error downstream: it
+		 * skips the power collapse and tries again later. -EAGAIN
+		 * gives the PM core that meaning; -ETIMEDOUT would set
+		 * runtime_error and leave the device unusable until unbind.
+		 */
+		if (IS_IRIS1(hdev->core))
+			return -EAGAIN;
 		return ret;
 	}
 
diff -ruN a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/hfi_venus_io.h b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/hfi_venus_io.h
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/hfi_venus_io.h
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/hfi_venus_io.h
@@ -54,6 +54,11 @@
 #define CPU_CS_VCICMD				0x20
 #define CPU_CS_VCICMD_ARP_OFF			BIT(0)
 
+/* IRIS1: the DSP (CVP) view of the HFI queue table */
+#define CPU_CS_VMIMSG				0x34
+#define CPU_CS_VMIMSGAG0			0x38
+#define CPU_CS_VMIMSGAG1			0x3c
+
 #define SFR_ADDR				0x5c
 #define MMAP_ADDR				0x60
 #define UC_REGION_ADDR				0x64
diff -ruN a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/pm_helpers.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/pm_helpers.c
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/pm_helpers.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/pm_helpers.c
@@ -1045,11 +1045,27 @@
 		ret = core_clks_enable(core);
 		if (ret < 0 && pmctrl)
 			pm_runtime_put_sync(pmctrl);
+
+		/*
+		 * IRIS1: the firmware drives the video core and the CVP from
+		 * the moment it boots. Downstream enables every GDSC (mvsc,
+		 * mvs0, mvs1) and hands them to hardware control before
+		 * loading it. Powered per session as on the sc7180, this
+		 * firmware answers SYS_INIT and then never goes idle nor
+		 * answers a session (measured 2026-09-19). Sessions still only
+		 * take core 1 (vcodec_num = 1); this just keeps both blocks
+		 * powered and under hardware control while the core is on.
+		 */
+		if (!ret && IS_IRIS1(core))
+			ret = poweron_coreid(core, VIDC_CORE_ID_1 | VIDC_CORE_ID_2);
 	} else {
 		/* Drop the performance state vote */
 		if (core->opp_pmdomain)
 			dev_pm_opp_set_rate(dev, 0);
 
+		if (IS_IRIS1(core))
+			poweroff_coreid(core, VIDC_CORE_ID_1 | VIDC_CORE_ID_2);
+
 		core_clks_disable(core);
 
 		ret = core_resets_reset(core);
